1b:T55d,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","@id":"https://www.outbrick.site/blog/when-to-play-and-when-to-pause/#article","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.outbrick.site/blog/when-to-play-and-when-to-pause"},"headline":"When to play—and when to put the phone down","description":"A candid guide to fitting games around sleep, attention, and the rest of a real day.","image":["https://www.outbrick.site/blog/when-to-play-and-when-to-pause.png"],"datePublished":"2026-09-04","dateModified":"2026-09-04","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"OutBrick Editorial Desk","description":"The OutBrick Editorial Desk turns player research, accessibility practice, and game-making lessons into useful, readable notes."},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"OutBrick","url":"https://www.outbrick.site","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.outbrick.site/icon.png"}},"articleSection":"Player habits","keywords":"healthy play, sleep, gaming habits, well-being","citation":["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2854707/","https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8216490/","https://www.who.int/news-room/questions-and-answers/item/addictive-behaviours-gaming-disorder","https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.241174","https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.220411"]}14:["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$1b"}}]
15:["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"OutBrick\",\"item\":\"https://www.outbrick.site\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Journal\",\"item\":\"https://www.outbrick.site/blog\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"When to play—and when to put the phone down\",\"item\":\"https://www.outbrick.site/blog/when-to-play-and-when-to-pause\"}]}"}}]
16:["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Does OutBrick recommend a specific daily play limit?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"No. People and contexts differ. We recommend paying attention to sleep, obligations, and whether you feel in control of your play.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Is gaming disorder the same as playing every day?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"No. WHO’s definition focuses on impaired control, priority over other activities, continuation despite negative consequences, and significant impairment over time.\"}}]}"}}]
17:["$","div",null,{"className":"article-body","children":[["$","section","sleep-is-a-real-design-constraint",{"id":"sleep-is-a-real-design-constraint","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Sleep is a real design constraint"}],[["$","p","In a controlled study of adolescents, playing a video game for 50 minutes before bed delayed sleep onset compared with watching a DVD. A separate prolonged-session experiment used different games and found changes in sleep efficiency and next-morning word recall. The results are specific to the conditions studied, but they support a sensible boundary: intense or stimulating play right before bed may not be the best fit for everyone.",{"children":"In a controlled study of adolescents, playing a video game for 50 minutes before bed delayed sleep onset compared with watching a DVD. A separate prolonged-session experiment used different games and found changes in sleep efficiency and next-morning word recall. The results are specific to the conditions studied, but they support a sensible boundary: intense or stimulating play right before bed may not be the best fit for everyone."}],["$","p","The honest design response is not to label all games harmful. It is to make stopping easy, avoid pretending that a late-night loop has no cost, and give players enough information to make their own choice.",{"children":"The honest design response is not to label all games harmful. It is to make stopping easy, avoid pretending that a late-night loop has no cost, and give players enough information to make their own choice."}]],null,null,["$","p",null,{"className":"article-source-note","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Research trail"}],[["$","a","sleep-2010",{"href":"#reference-sleep-2010","aria-label":"Jump to source: Weaver et al. (2010)","children":["[",1,"]"]}]]]}]]}],["$","section","problematic-is-not-the-same-as-ordinary",{"id":"problematic-is-not-the-same-as-ordinary","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Problematic is not the same as ordinary"}],[["$","p","A systematic review and meta-analysis found an association between problematic gaming and shorter sleep duration, with considerable variation between studies. That variability matters because the evidence concerns a pattern of gaming linked to impairment, not everyone who plays for fun.",{"children":"A systematic review and meta-analysis found an association between problematic gaming and shorter sleep duration, with considerable variation between studies. That variability matters because the evidence concerns a pattern of gaming linked to impairment, not everyone who plays for fun."}],["$","p","The World Health Organization describes gaming disorder through impaired control, increasing priority given to gaming, and continuation despite negative consequences, severe enough to cause significant impairment and usually evident for at least twelve months. It is a clinical definition, not a synonym for “I played longer than planned once.”",{"children":"The World Health Organization describes gaming disorder through impaired control, increasing priority given to gaming, and continuation despite negative consequences, severe enough to cause significant impairment and usually evident for at least twelve months. It is a clinical definition, not a synonym for “I played longer than planned once.”"}]],null,null,["$","p",null,{"className":"article-source-note","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Research trail"}],[["$","a","sleep-review-2021",{"href":"#reference-sleep-review-2021","aria-label":"Jump to source: Kristensen et al. (2021)","children":["[",2,"]"]}],"$L1c"]]}]]}],"$L1d","$L1e"]}]
18:["$","section",null,{"id":"faq","className":"article-faq","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-kicker","children":"Questions, answered"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"A few useful answers"}],[["$","details","Does OutBrick recommend a specific daily play limit?",{"children":[["$","summary",null,{"children":"Does OutBrick recommend a specific daily play limit?"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"No. People and contexts differ. We recommend paying attention to sleep, obligations, and whether you feel in control of your play."}]]}],["$","details","Is gaming disorder the same as playing every day?",{"children":[["$","summary",null,{"children":"Is gaming disorder the same as playing every day?"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"No. WHO’s definition focuses on impaired control, priority over other activities, continuation despite negative consequences, and significant impairment over time."}]]}]]]}]
19:["$","section",null,{"id":"references","className":"article-references","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-kicker","children":[["$","$Lf",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M15 3h6v6","key":"1q9fwt"}],["path",{"d":"M10 14 21 3","key":"gplh6r"}],["path",{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6","key":"a6xqqp"}]],"className":"lucide-external-link","size":14}]," APA 7 reference trail"]}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"References"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"article-reference-intro","children":"The claims in this story are grounded in the sources below. External links open the source in a new tab; first-party histories and editorial explainers are labelled by context in the article."}],["$","ol",null,{"children":[["$","li","sleep-2010",{"id":"reference-sleep-2010","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Weaver, D. J., Gradisar, M. J., Dohnt, J. D., Lovato, H., & Douglas, M. (2010). The effect of presleep video-game playing on adolescent sleep. Journal of Clinical Sleep Medicine, 6(2), 184–189."}]," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2854707/","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":["Read source ",["$","$Lf",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$19:props:children:0:props:children:0:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-external-link","size":13}]]}]]}],["$","li","sleep-review-2021",{"id":"reference-sleep-review-2021","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Kristensen, H. E., Pallesen, S., King, D. L., et al. (2021). Problematic gaming and sleep: A systematic review and meta-analysis. Frontiers in Psychiatry, 12, 675237."}]," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8216490/","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":["Read source ",["$","$Lf",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$19:props:children:0:props:children:0:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-external-link","size":13}]]}]]}],["$","li","who-gaming-disorder",{"id":"reference-who-gaming-disorder","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"World Health Organization. (2020, October 22). Addictive behaviours: Gaming disorder."}]," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://www.who.int/news-room/questions-and-answers/item/addictive-behaviours-gaming-disorder","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":["Read source ",["$","$Lf",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$19:props:children:0:props:children:0:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-external-link","size":13}]]}]]}],["$","li","gaming-fit-2025",{"id":"reference-gaming-fit-2025","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Ballou, N., Vuorre, M., Hakman, T., Magnusson, K., & Przybylski, A. K. (2025). Perceived value of video games, but not hours played, predicts mental well-being in casual adult Nintendo players. Royal Society Open Science, 12(3)."}]," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.241174","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":["Read source ",["$","$Lf",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$19:props:children:0:props:children:0:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-external-link","size":13}]]}]]}],["$","li","time-wellbeing-2022",{"id":"reference-time-wellbeing-2022","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Vuorre, M., Johannes, N., Magnusson, K., & Przybylski, A. K. (2022). Time spent playing video games is unlikely to impact well-being. Royal Society Open Science, 9(7), 220411."}]," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.220411","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":["Read source ",["$","$Lf",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$19:props:children:0:props:children:0:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-external-link","size":13}]]}]]}]]}]]}]
1a:["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-card-body","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-card-meta","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Game craft"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","$Lf",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$1:props:children:2:props:children:1:props:children:3:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-clock3 lucide-clock-3","size":13}]," ","7 min read"]}]]}],["$","h3",null,{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/blog/kinder-difficulty-curve","children":"How to build a kinder difficulty curve"}]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Challenge should stretch the player’s attention without making the relationship with the game feel brittle."}],["$","a",null,{"className":"blog-read-link","href":"/blog/kinder-difficulty-curve","children":["Read story ",["$","$Lf",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$1:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-chevron-right","size":16}]]}]]}]
